---
permalink: /quay/
title: Quay — Your local dev stack in one menu bar
description: Start, stop and monitor local dev servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents from one macOS menu bar app. Free and open source.
keywords: quay, macos menu bar app, dev services manager, localhost ports, docker, homebrew
generate_social_image: false
image: /assets/img/quay/social-preview.png
---

{% extends "./_layouts/base.njk" %}
{% from "components/desktop-frame.njk" import desktopFrame %}

{% block custom_style %}
	{% set css_product %}{% include "css/product.css" %}{% endset %}
	{{ css_product | cssmin | safe }}
{% endblock %}

{% set repo = "https://github.com/manustays/quay" %}
{% set download = "https://github.com/manustays/quay/releases/latest" %}

{% block main %}
<div class="product">

	{# ---------- Hero ---------- #}
	<section class="block product-hero">
		<div class="product-hero-grid">
			<div class="product-hero-copy">
				<div class="product-hero-head">
					<img class="product-logo" src="/assets/img/quay/logo.svg" alt="" width="88" height="88" />
					<div class="product-hero-titles">
						<div class="product-wordmark">Quay</div>
						<div class="product-pronounce mono">/kiː/ · where your ports come in</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h1 class="product-headline">Your entire local dev stack.<br><span class="hl">One menu bar.</span></h1>

				<p class="product-lede">Start, stop and monitor dev servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents from one lightweight macOS app — with live health, CPU and memory, and port-conflict detection.</p>

				<div class="product-cta">
					<a class="button" href="{{ download }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						{% svgico 'arrow-circle-down' %}Download for macOS
					</a>
					<a class="button secondary" href="{{ repo }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
						{% svgico 'github' %}View on GitHub
					</a>
				</div>

				<p class="product-note">
					<svg class="product-note-ico" width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><line x1="12" y1="11" x2="12" y2="16"/><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="0.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg>
					Preview builds aren't notarized yet — macOS may ask for one confirmation in Privacy &amp; Security. Fully open source under MIT.
				</p>

				<ul class="product-badges">
					<li>macOS</li>
					<li>Rust + TypeScript</li>
					<li>Tauri v2</li>
					<li>MIT</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="product-hero-visual">
				{{ desktopFrame("/assets/img/quay/popup.png", "Quay menu bar popup listing running dev services with live status, CPU and memory metrics.", transparent=true) }}
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Positioning callout ---------- #}
	<section class="block product-callout product-highlight-bg product-callout-text">
			<span class="product-callout-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			Not just a port monitor — <span class="hl">a control center for everything running locally.</span>
	</section>

	<div class="product-highlight-bg">

		{# ---------- High-value workflows ---------- #}
		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="product-section-title">What a good local day looks like</h2>
			<ul class="product-workflows">
				<li class="product-workflow">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'flow-bolt' %}</span>
					<h3>Start your stack in seconds</h3>
					<p>Your frontend, API and Redis sit together as one group — start them from the menu bar in seconds, no terminal tabs to hunt down.</p>
					<ul class="product-workflow-tags">
						<li>Project servers</li>
						<li>Homebrew services</li>
						<li>Auto-detection</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li class="product-workflow">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-radar' %}</span>
					<h3>Find what stole your port</h3>
					<p>Port radar spots the unmanaged process on a port. Open it in the browser to identify it, then adopt it into Quay or terminate it.</p>
					<ul class="product-workflow-tags">
						<li>Port radar</li>
						<li>One-click browser</li>
						<li>Live status &amp; health</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li class="product-workflow">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-metrics' %}</span>
					<h3>Keep heavy services visible</h3>
					<p>Watch CPU, memory, uptime and health right from the menu bar — no need to open Activity Monitor.</p>
					<ul class="product-workflow-tags">
						<li>Resource metrics</li>
						<li>Live status &amp; health</li>
						<li>Unified management</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		{# ---------- Four kinds of service ---------- #}
		<section class="block">
			<!-- p class="product-eyebrow">Everything running locally</p -->
			<h2 class="product-kinds-title">Four kinds of service. One place.</h2>
			<ul class="product-kinds">
				<li class="product-kind">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-services' %}</span>
					<h3>Project servers</h3>
					<p>Next.js, Vite, Django, Rails — auto-detected from your project config and grouped into one stack.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-kind">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-brew' %}</span>
					<h3>Homebrew services</h3>
					<p>Redis, Postgres, MySQL, MongoDB. Start and stop brew services without touching the terminal.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-kind">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-docker' %}</span>
					<h3>Docker containers</h3>
					<p>See and control running containers alongside everything else — no separate dashboard.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-kind">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-terminal' %}</span>
					<h3>Terminal &amp; AI agents</h3>
					<p>Keep long-running agents like Claude Code visible, with live start/stop status right in the menu bar.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		{# ---------- Comparison ---------- #}
		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="product-section-title">More than a port monitor</h2>
			<p class="product-compare-lede">Most tools stop at listening ports. Quay manages the whole stack — the rows below are where it pulls ahead.</p>

			<div class="product-compare-card">
				<div class="product-compare-scroll">
					<table class="product-compare">
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th scope="col">Capability</th>
								<th scope="col">Typical port monitor</th>
								<th scope="col" class="product-compare-us">
									<img class="product-compare-logo" src="/assets/img/quay/logo.svg" alt="" width="20" height="20" />Quay
								</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							{% set compareRows = [
								{ cap: "See listening ports",          typical: "Yes",  edge: false },
								{ cap: "Kill port / process",          typical: "Yes",  edge: false },
								{ cap: "Manage project servers",       typical: "Some", edge: false },
								{ cap: "Homebrew services",            typical: "—",    edge: true  },
								{ cap: "Docker containers",            typical: "Some", edge: true  },
								{ cap: "Terminal &amp; AI agents",     typical: "—",    edge: true  },
								{ cap: "CPU &amp; memory per service", typical: "—",    edge: true  },
								{ cap: "HTTP health checks",           typical: "Some", edge: false },
								{ cap: "Auto-detect project config",   typical: "Some", edge: false },
								{ cap: "Adopt unmanaged processes",    typical: "Some", edge: false },
								{ cap: "Group full stacks",            typical: "—",    edge: true  }
							] %}
							{% for row in compareRows %}
								<tr{% if row.edge %} class="is-edge"{% endif %}>
									<th scope="row">{{ row.cap | safe }}</th>
									<td class="product-compare-typical">{{ row.typical | safe }}</td>
									<td class="product-compare-yes">
										<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'check' %}</span>
										<span class="visually-hidden">Yes</span>
									</td>
								</tr>
							{% endfor %}
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{# ---------- Features ---------- # }
		<section class="block">
			<h2 class="product-section-title">One dock for every local service</h2>
			<ul class="product-features">
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-services' %}</span>
					<h3>Unified management</h3>
					<p>Node &amp; Python servers, Homebrew services, Docker containers and terminal agents — all in one list.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-health' %}</span>
					<h3>Live status &amp; health</h3>
					<p>Process-liveness checks plus HTTP health verification so you know what's actually up.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-metrics' %}</span>
					<h3>Resource metrics</h3>
					<p>Real-time CPU and memory usage per service, right in the menu bar.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-browser' %}</span>
					<h3>One-click browser</h3>
					<p>Open <code>localhost:&lt;port&gt;</code> for any running service without hunting for the port.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-radar' %}</span>
					<h3>Port radar</h3>
					<p>Detects unmanaged dev servers on your machine — adopt them into Quay or terminate them.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-stack' %}</span>
					<h3>Stack-aware</h3>
					<p>Recognises frameworks like Vite, Next, Django and Rails and shows the right tech-stack icon.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-favorites' %}</span>
					<h3>Organised your way</h3>
					<p>Favorites, search and collapsible groups keep a long list of services tidy.</p>
				</li>
				<li class="product-feature">
					<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'feature-detect' %}</span>
					<h3>Auto-detection</h3>
					<p>Reads start commands and ports from <code>package.json</code>, <code>requirements.txt</code> and <code>.env</code>.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section> #}

	</div>

	{# ---------- How it works ---------- #}
	<section class="block bg-shaded">
		<h2 class="product-section-title">Up and running in a minute</h2>
		<ol class="product-steps">
			<li class="product-step">
				<h3>Install</h3>
				<p>Download the latest <code>.dmg</code> and drag Quay to <code>/Applications</code>.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-step">
				<h3>Add a service</h3>
				<p>Hit <code>+ Add</code>, pick a project folder — Quay auto-fills the start command and port.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-step">
				<h3>Control it</h3>
				<p>Start, stop, open in the browser or jump to a terminal — all from the menu bar.</p>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Open-source trust ---------- #}
	<section class="block product-trust">
		<h2 class="product-section-title">Open source you can trust</h2>
		<ul class="product-trust-grid">
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-license' %}</span>
				<h3>MIT licensed</h3>
				<p>A permissive license — use, fork and ship it however you like.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-local' %}</span>
				<h3>Fully local</h3>
				<p>Your services and settings never leave your Mac.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-no-account' %}</span>
				<h3>No account</h3>
				<p>No sign-up, no login. Download it and go.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-no-telemetry' %}</span>
				<h3>No telemetry</h3>
				<p>Zero tracking, zero analytics, zero phone-home.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-code' %}</span>
				<h3>Rust + TypeScript</h3>
				<p>A Tauri app: a fast Rust core with a TypeScript interface.</p>
			</li>
			<li class="product-kind">
				<span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'trust-lightweight' %}</span>
				<h3>Lightweight</h3>
				<p>Native and lean — no Electron, no bundled browser.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<div class="product-trust-links">
			<a href="{{ repo }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View source</a>
			<a href="{{ download }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Current release</a>
			<a href="{{ repo }}/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Contributions welcome</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Support / sponsor ---------- #}
	<section class="block product-support bg-shaded">
			<span class="product-support-ico" aria-hidden="true">{% svgico 'heart' %}</span>
			<h2 class="product-section-title product-support-title">Enjoying Quay?</h2>
			<p class="product-support-text">Quay is free and open source, built in my spare time. If it saves you time, a one-time sponsorship — or even a quick star — genuinely helps and keeps me motivated.</p>
			<div class="product-cta product-support-cta">
				<a class="button sponsor" href="https://github.com/sponsors/manustays?frequency=one-time" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					{% svgico 'heart' %}Sponsor on GitHub
				</a>
				<a class="button secondary" href="{{ repo }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
					{% svgico 'github' %}Star on GitHub
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="product-support-note">No pressure — Quay stays free either way.</p>
	</section>

	{# ---------- Closing CTA ---------- #}
	<section class="block product-closing">
		<div class="product-cta">
			<a class="button" href="{{ download }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
				{% svgico 'arrow-circle-down' %}Download for macOS
			</a>
		</div>
		<p class="product-license">MIT © 2026 Kumar Abhishek</p>
	</section>

</div>
{% endblock %}
